  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Passenger Information Display",
    "overview": "The profile is a run of real-looking PIS hardware: amber LEDs on black glass, inside charcoal housings that carry a silkscreened model strip. Every visible letter is a lit dot drawn from one hand-set 5x7 face, so each board reads at once as a transit sign and as a terminal printing bits. The page is a sequence of four displays in story order (destination sign, departures board, service updates, terminus), each a full-width 880-unit SVG, with GitHub's own Markdown carrying only the short prose and the link between them.\n\nThe world is dense, mechanical and flat-lit. Nothing glows, nothing is graded, and nothing moves smoothly: text steps one dot at a time and pages hard-cut, the way firmware drives a matrix. The unlit grid is always visible, because a real panel's dead LEDs are part of how it looks. The only hue outside amber is the green live pip, and it means exactly one thing.\n\nAll design tokens live in `scripts/build_displays.py`; the SVGs in `assets/` are generated output and are never hand-edited.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One colour of light (#FFB000) on one glass, with the off-state grid always drawn.",
      "One bitmap face, proportional, with descenders, a bold variant and integer scaling only.",
      "Two LED pitches (4 for signs, 3 for boards) and one square-pixel silkscreen pitch (2.6).",
      "Stepped motion only: steps() scrolling at 30 dots/s, hard-cut pages, on/off blinks.",
      "Every display is complete when static; motion is decoration over a still frame."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Emitter Rule",
        "body": "Inside the glass there is amber and dead amber, nothing else. A second LED colour would make it a different display.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Green Means Live Rule",
        "body": "Live green marks real in-service status and is used for nothing decorative: no green text, no green accents, no green bars.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Face Rule",
        "body": "Every character on every display comes from the 5x7 face. A missing glyph is added to `FONT_SRC` as a bitmap; it is never substituted with a system font, an emoji or an icon.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Integer Scale Rule",
        "body": "Scale is 1, 2 or 3 whole dots per dot. A size that needs a fractional scale is the wrong size; pick another pitch or another scale.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cold LED Rule",
        "body": "A lit dot is a flat round-capped stroke (width 0.74 of pitch). No blur, glow, halo or gradient on any dot.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** draw every character with the 5x7 face, adding glyphs to `FONT_SRC` as bitmaps when needed.",
      "**Do** keep the dead LED grid visible behind every lit layer.",
      "**Do** move text only in whole-dot steps (steps() timing, 30 dots/s) and change pages by hard cut.",
      "**Do** make every display complete with animation off: the still line, page A and the knocked-out cursor are the reduced-motion frame.",
      "**Do** put the information of every display in its alt text and `<title>`.",
      "**Do** knock content out of lit blocks (route badge, line numbers) instead of using a second colour."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a second LED colour, a gradient, or any glow or blur on the dots.",
      "**Don't** use live green for anything except a real live or in-service pip.",
      "**Don't** use fractional scales or set any text inside the glass below pitch 3 at 1x.",
      "**Don't** add eased, smooth or sub-dot motion; no fades between pages.",
      "**Don't** add shields-style badges, stats cards or typing-SVG headers; the komarev visitor counter is a retained product requirement, not a pattern to extend.",
      "**Don't** pad a board with invented facts or ratings; an unknown is shown as \"Soon\" or omitted."
    ]
  }
